From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 19:21:49 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 89/89] server: an adaptive context window shares a token budget
 among the active chats, above a floor

A served engine whose KV is a shared pool (and whose idle chats park on NVMe) can give one chat its whole window
while few are active, but one long chat may then take the pool from many. TENSORFOLD_CONTEXT_BUDGET turns on a
window that follows load: budget / active chats, rounded down to 256 tokens, between TENSORFOLD_CONTEXT_FLOOR and
the static window. A chat is named by its opening 512 tokens past the shared system prefix and counts as active from
its second request within TENSORFOLD_CONTEXT_HOLD_S (300) of the last one, so a burst of one-shot requests (a
benchmark, quick API calls) lowers no one's window once it is done; the requests in flight bound the count from
below. Background requests are not noted. Off (budget 0) by default: the static window, as before.
DeepSeek-V4.1 reads the same settings as TF_DSV41_CONTEXT_* (what its launchers forward), each ignored while
its TENSORFOLD_ name is set.

The window binds where chat and completion prompts are checked (chat.prepare): an over-window prompt gets the same
OpenAI-worded context_length_exceeded 400 ("... while this server serves several chats"), and the reply limit is
capped to the lowered room, so a request never reserves past it. Admitted requests keep their reservation.
/v1/models keeps the static window; the open /health body adds context {window, active_chats, budget, floor}.

Tests: the window's arithmetic (1-4 chats at 1M of a 4M budget, 8 at 512K, 16+ at the 256K floor, page rounding,
off by default), chat keys, counting from the second request, a one-shot burst that leaves a long chat its window,
hold expiry and capacity; and chat preparations on a fixture tokenizer where one-shot and background requests leave
the long chat its window, a returning second chat halves it and refuses the first chat's long prompt, and a floor at
the budget keeps the whole window, under either set of names, and a TENSORFOLD_ name wins over its TF_DSV41_ one.
